            "parts": [
              "I followed Note 40 and continued the spatial-joining analysis.\n\nThe completed Sol manuscript revision matches its recorded hashes. My [focused review](/Users/ebbaker/Documents/shifted-zeta-positivity/papers/investigations-5/01_heat_density_asymptotics/reviews/23_MI2_FOCUSED_ANALYTICAL_REVIEW_20261024.md) found no blocking integration issue within the inspected scope.\n\nThe new result is in [Note 42](/Users/ebbaker/Documents/shifted-zeta-positivity/papers/investigations-5/01_heat_density_asymptotics/notes/42_GAP_LOCALIZED_SPATIAL_DEFECTS_20261024.md): **place the spatial cutoff inside a zero-free gap of the explicit outer model.** I derived the additional curvature, potential and current terms while retaining the actual covariance. On a specified short time slab after the regulator switch, these transition terms admit bounds without an inverse regulator floor. Under the stated relative field-error assumptions, the largest new filtered local allowance is \\(O(\\log^3 X/X^2)\\).\n\nThis pays the **local transition defects**, not the complete approximation. Full averaging supports, root collars, effective source accuracy and finite construction cost still need payment. HDA-18 remains Gated.\n\n**Next: Analysis — Sol**, under the saved [HDA-18-AN01 handoff](/Users/ebbaker/Documents/shifted-zeta-positivity/papers/investigations-5/01_heat_density_asymptotics/research-progress/handoffs/HDA-18-AN01.md). Complete that comparison before expanding numerics.\n\n:::writing{variant=\"standard\" id=\"58241\"}\nFollow HDA-18-AN01 r1 and Note 42. Complete the full-support comparison for the fixed-gap spatial join, retaining all partition, nonholomorphic and heat defects and actual covariance. Give finite source/gap requirements or the precise failed estimate.\n:::"
